Cat Leather Jackets is a linear visual novel and music game about being a teenager in a punk rock band.

Follow Priya and her bandmates Ian and Dave as they get together to write and rehearse songs, try to find gigs and ultimately an audience for their music – all the while trying to find independence and figuring out what they want to do with their lives.

The game features ten original tracks with gameplay segments, intertwining a kinetic novel style narrative with an indie comic book/ graphic novel aesthetic.

- A Story Mode : get to know Priya, Ian and Dave and play CLJ's setlist at their first gig;

- In Story Mode, win or lose in the Punk Mode . Just want to enjoy the story? Try the Default Mode .

- Play any and all unlocked songs for the highest score in the Practice Mode ;

- Unlock all Steam Achievements;

- And enjoy ten completely original punk, ska and alternative rock playable beatmaps .

Use the rules of the famous Tower of Hanoi puzzle,
where a larger piece cannot be on top of a smaller one.

Every move the piece Spins clockwise changing its pattern,
in most of the cases you have to do one or more extra moves to get the right pattern when stacking. Features:

- 50 carefully designed levels;

- Original soundtrack inspired by Synthwave classics and some cyberpunk touches;

- Relaxing gameplay, perfect for those looking for casual puzzle;

- Beautiful futuristic art.

The Witch's Cauldron – a medieval witch simulator from the young indie team Harvey Games.

You’ll practice your craft in a town where good rumors spread just as fast as bad ones, with the latter quickly reaching the ears of inquisitors. Balancing your popularity among townsfolk and the inquisitors’ growing attention is essential for survival here. And if your witch’s intuition tells you the end is near, you can always find refuge in another town—there are plenty nearby.

But that’s for the future. For now, bards, vampires, innkeepers, and even the king himself come to pay their respects! Fulfill their requests, brew potions, but remember: every good or evil deed will bring inevitable consequences.

- Over 60 unique characters, each with their own story and multiple playthrough options;

- A vast array of potions, each capable of leading to a unique story outcome;

- A variety of witch skins that unlock unique quests, present challenges, and subtly alter gameplay;

- 6 main story endings that affect not only your life but also the entire kingdom;

- Numerous nighttime events reflecting the outcomes of your choices;

- High replayability, allowing you to explore the world, uncover the witch’s past, and understand the kingdom’s morals.
Each day, locals will visit you. Some come seeking healing, others out of curiosity, and some with a desire to engage in darker deeds. Their fates are in your hands—it’s up to you to decide how to handle them.
With your choice of potions, you influence the course of events. However, only a few basic potions are available from the start; you’ll need to unlock new and more complex ones by mixing ingredients or obtaining recipes and hints from NPCs.

Unlocked potions, no matter how each story ends, will carry over to your next life cycle. The abundance of potions and story twists allows for a highly variable playthrough experience. Some endings, potions, and game mechanics will only be available after completing the main story once or reaching certain game events that conclude the story.

Embark on an enlightening journey into the world of coding with "SirKwitz," an introductory educational game designed to demystify the fundamentals of programming. This beginner-friendly game is a perfect entry point for young people and adults new to the field, offering a hands-on approach to learning basic programming, through a series of engaging puzzles. Over four main topics, each comprised of seven levels, players will explore key coding concepts: base logic, loops, orientation, sequences, and debugging.



"SirKwitz" combines learning with enjoyable gameplay, featuring a simple yet intuitive UI used to puppeteer our cute little robot which will help you translate programming concepts into instant action. The game focuses on developing core skills essential for budding programmers, such as problem analysis, spatial orientation, logic, and computational thinking, along with fostering attributes like focus and perseverance.



Key Features:

• Especially tailored for those who think "programming" is a scary word;

• Engaging, story-driven gameplay;

• Simple yet complicated puzzles teaching core programming concepts;

• Simple, clean & intuitive user interface, suitable for both young learners and adults alike.

SKYSAVIOR Helicopter Services is a helicopter game developed by the Código Justo team. In the game, players take on the role of a helicopter pilot, fulfilling objectives transmitted by the operations center.

OBJECTIVE

The main objective of SKYSAVIOR Helicopter Services is to complete as many calls as possible while facing the challenges presented in each mission. Players are rewarded with points and unlock new helicopters, upgrades, and missions as they progress through the game. The ultimate goal is to become an elite rescue pilot and master all aspects of helicopter flying in extreme environments.

